<title>USA: Simula says got $65 mln in new business in Q1.</title>
<headline>Simula says got $65 mln in new business in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>PHOENIX 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Simula Inc said Tuesday it has captured in excess of $65 million in new business during the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The company said it expects &quot;significant revenues&quot; in 1997 from airline seat orders and its inflatable tubular restraint system.</p>
<p>&quot;Likewise, the company expects to start deliveries of the bulkhead airbag system (BABS), the new military parachute, the IBAHRS and the CABS products this year,&quot; Simula president Don Townsend said in a statement.</p>
</text>
